From: AutoBuild-H5000M-Openwrt <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sing-box: pin to 1.12.25 so the LuCI front-ends can drive it

sing-box 1.13.0 removed the legacy inbound fields. HomeProxy still emits
them on master and dev, so the daemon refuses to start with:

  FATAL decode config at /var/run/homeproxy/sing-box-c.json: inbounds[1]:
  legacy inbound fields are deprecated in sing-box 1.11.0 and removed in 1.13.0

PassWall2 fails the same way. 1.12.25 is the last release accepting them.
The enabled tags are clash_api and gvisor; 1.12.25 supports both.

---
 feeds/packages/net/sing-box/Makefile | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/feeds/packages/net/sing-box/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/packages/net/sing-box/Makefile
@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=sing-box
-PKG_VERSION:=1.14.0
+PKG_VERSION:=1.12.25
 PKG_RELEASE:=1
 
 PKG_SOURCE:=$(PKG_NAME)-$(PKG_VERSION).tar.gz
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://codeload.github.com/SagerNet/sing-box/tar.gz/v$(PKG_VERSION)?
-PKG_HASH:=87baf6852e37941cbe40bdd94bec81c957c88a56751cecd6bbf0e6108bc69398
+PKG_HASH:=881435f07b5ab8170ccf3cb69e87130759521dc0ed1ae4bfeacbe7772a93a158
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-3.0-or-later
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=LICENSE
